      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This has been happening in a world of mine I updated yesterday.  With the help of a friend on live while I was on the beta (installed today, so I should have the up-to-date version), I was able to join the world when I created it on beta, but was unable to join it when my friend created it on live.\n\nThis is not an issue on the older version of my world.\n\nAn error I get in my world when I get kicked out:\n\nError      -  [Behaviour] Failed to collected metadata on /NetworkedPlayerManager [3]/PlayerPositionSync/PlayerReviver\n\nObject reference not set to an instance of an object.\n\nNetworkedPlayerManager is a manual synched PlayerObject (no persistence).  PlayerPositionSync is a NoVariableSync child of NetworkedPlayerManager.  PlayerReviver is a NoVariableSync child of PlayerPositionSync.\n\nNetworkedPlayerManager has another child object that is manual sync that didn't appear to throw an error.\n\nHere is a working version of my world: https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_32a0e2ec-cb81-4367-a93a-31f7ee7324a4/info\n\nAnd this is the version of my world that has the issue: https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_afa6359c-0679-46d1-9ae7-9f4e648650c3/info",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
