      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Doing a bunch more testing and seeing if I could get things to work I had a case where I was able to join the world on Quest Live when PC Beta had created it. I then attempted to rejoin on quest and was able to do so without issue. At this point, the PC user recreated the world and the quest user was no longer able to join it, getting the World version error, even though the world had not changed.\n\nI have verbose logs from both sides of the testing I can provide if needed.\n\nFor my testing tonight, I:\n\n1. Ensured all networked objects were the same in both versions\n\n2. Downgraded SDK to 3.9.0 from 3.9.1b1\n\nI had the same results when connecting from Quest live to the world. When connecting from Quest Beta it did work.\n\nFor a final test, I reenabled one (not-synced) item so the two platforms were no longer the same the same and it still worked.\n\nTesting was done using my WIP world: wrld_5001fb52-6fbd-42a8-8f11-5b00a21c861d; there is a button on the backside of the front counter which will log (to the best of my current knowledge of UdonSharp), what it thinks its NetworkIDs are.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
